SmartTar v0.4.0

Use SmartTar to install supported Linux app downloads and add menu shortcuts.

After installing the package, run smarttar --migrate as your normal desktop user
to move an earlier user installation to this package. For a new installation,
run smarttar --setup to select SmartTar as your download handler.

Open .tar.gz, .tgz, or .AppImage downloads with SmartTar. For executable
AppImages, right-click and choose Open With SmartTar if double-click runs the
download directly.

When the signed SmartTar repository is configured, normal system updates also
update SmartTar. A package file installed on its own does not add that source.
The programs installed through SmartTar have their own separate update needs.

Before removing the SmartTar package, run smarttar --restore-association as
your normal desktop user. Then remove the package with your software manager.
Programs previously installed through SmartTar are kept.

Report a problem: https://github.com/HaytamElbouhmidi/smarttar/issues
